From a78af461b6bf803c60927d90f33f42b5f121fe9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] Holdout recorded (gate invalid: G7); A5 ablation now
 replaces the routing choke point

The single holdout run of the frozen candidate (7f37551, world M seed 101)
scored 120/120 with 0 disclosures, but the architecture gate failed G7: three
hypothesis claims' root counts changed after the asker views were captured
without a version bump or revision row (KnowledgeService.sync_support_sync).
Under contract section 8 the score is not published as full-system accuracy.
Central baseline source 114/120, single 70/120.

Post-holdout harness change (ablations only, reviewed): A5 now replaces
Authorizer._can_route, which candidate_holders and can_route_many call
directly, and records how often it was reached; with it G4 fails (13,554
replay denials). Dev ablation, run and dev baseline result files are added
under results/runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
